Removes draft 53's landing rule from `FolderState::applied` (6077a6b): a
failed commit whose carried observation is exactly what the commit would
have left no longer counts as its landing. A reset that landed before a
crash took its report then fails its retry's guard and is dropped, never
announced, so a peer its window refused never asks again (DESIGN.md §7.5
step 6, §13). Seeds 821 and 1113 (--nodes 2 --steps 200) showed it on
main; with draft 52's carried observation in place their histories no
longer reach it, and no seed does in 45,300 run with this patch (0 to
1,999 and 76,000, 86,000 and 96,000 slices at the defaults, and 0 to
19,999 in two-node and in three-node worlds at 200 steps), so the fix's
unit test stands in for a pinned seed.

test: delocal-engine folder::tests::a_reset_whose_retry_finds_its_own_work_has_landed

